      "math_academy_id": "e-4716",
      "problem": "Is \n$\\begin{aligned}E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}$ \nan elementary matrix?",
      "worked_solution": "An elementary matrix is a matrix obtained from the identity matrix by applying exactly one elementary row operation.\n\nThe given matrix $E$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from $I_2$ by applying the elementary row operation $R_2:= R_2+(-5) R_1,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$",
